# Branch Naming

Format: `<type>/<JIRA-ID>-<short-description>`

Valid type prefixes: `feature/`, `fix/`, `migration/`, `chore/`, `spike/`, `hotfix/`

```
feature/PAI-142-add-rate-limiter      ✅
fix/PAI-211-null-pointer-login        ✅
add-otp-verification                  ❌ no type, no Jira ID
feature/customer-management           ❌ no Jira ID
VehicleManagement                     ❌ no type, no Jira ID
```

# Commit Messages

Every commit subject must start with the Jira ticket ID:

```
PAI-142: add rate limiter middleware   ✅
wip                                    ❌
misc fixes                             ❌
updates                                ❌
```

- Use the ticket actively being worked: Story, Task, Sub-task, or Bug. Never an Epic.
- Describe what changed; vague subjects are rejected in review.
- Squash before merging to `main`, and the squashed commit must still carry the Jira ID.
- CI rejects any commit without a valid Jira ID, so a missing ID fails the build.

# Standalone QA Epics

Create a separate epic when QA work can be independently released and measured:

- General test automation frameworks (Selenium grid, API test harness) → Engineering Excellence → Test Automation
- Regression suite overhauls not tied to one feature → Engineering Excellence → Test Automation

Never use `Product Features` as the Work Category for a QA-only epic.
